{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5296) to implement `cmd/comm` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically covering requirements R1.1-R1.4 from srd029-comm. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/comm/main.go` (the comm utility implementation) and `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` (differential tests against GNU's gcomm). Only the R1 requirement group (three-column comparison output) is in scope; R2 (column suppression), R3 (order checking/output delimiter), and R4 (exit codes/SIGPIPE) are NOT in scope but the code should be structured for later extension.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **comm utility**: Compares two sorted files line by line, producing three-column output (file1-only, file2-only, common)\n   - **Differential testing**: Using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` to compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary `gcomm`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main()\n   - **Sorted input assumption**: comm does NOT sort inputs; files must be pre-sorted\n   - **LC_ALL=C byte-for-byte comparison**: No locale collation\n   - **Three-column output format**: Column 1 = no indent, Column 2 = one tab, Column 3 = two tabs\n   - **Lexicographic merge**: Lines less than counterpart go to their file's column; equal lines go to column 3\n   - **File exhaustion handling**: Remaining lines go to appropriate column when one file ends\n   - **40-line function limit**, **500-line file limit**, **write all files before building**\n   - **Copyright header**: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + SPDX\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd029-comm.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for comm utility, read to understand R1.1-R1.4 requirements\n     - R1.1: Read file1/file2 simultaneously; col1 (no indent), col2 (1 tab), col3 (2 tabs)\n     - R1.2: Lexicographic comparison determines column placement\n     - R1.3: Exhausted file → remaining lines to appropriate column\n     - R1.4: Byte-for-byte comparison, optional trailing newline doesn't affect comparison\n     - Non-goals: no sorting, no locale collation\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED INLINE in project_context)\n     - Key exports: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests` function, `BuildBinary` (in build.go), `NormalizeFunc`, `ComposeNormalizers`, `TimestampNormalizer`\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `Name string`, `Args []string`, `Stdin []byte`, `Env []string`, `WorkDir string`, `ExitCode int`, `Normalize []NormalizeFunc`, `ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)` runs each test as a subtest\n   \n   - **cmd/comm/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Must implement R1.1-R1.4 three-column comparison\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n     - Should be structured for later R2-R4 extension\n   \n   - **cmd/comm/comm_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests using `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gcomm\")`\n     - Skip gracefully if gcomm not installed\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; no code has been written or compiled.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full requirement scope for R1.1-R1.4\n   - No implementation work has begun yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt containing role definition, repository files list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement cmd/comm R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/comm/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 (three-column sorted file comparison)\n   - Create `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` with differential tests against gcomm\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/comm/` to verify compilation (AC3)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/comm/ -count=1` to verify tests pass or skip gracefully (AC4)\n   - Verify `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` is called at start of main (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`srd029-comm.yaml`) to understand the R1.1-R1.4 requirements for the comm utility. I was in the planning/review phase — step 1-2 of the task instructions (\"Review provided context\" and \"Plan approach\"). No code has been written yet. The next action would be to write both source files (`main.go` and `comm_test.go`) in one pass, then build and test.\n\n   Key implementation details gathered:\n   - comm reads two sorted files, merges them lexicographically\n   - Output: col1 (file1-only, no indent), col2 (file2-only, \"\\t\" prefix), col3 (common, \"\\t\\t\" prefix)\n   - When one file exhausted, drain remaining into appropriate column\n   - Byte-for-byte comparison under LC_ALL=C\n   - Must handle \"-\" as stdin (standard comm convention)\n   - Design for extensibility: R2 adds -1/-2/-3 flags, R3 adds --check-order/--nocheck-order/--output-delimiter, R4 adds exit codes\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/comm/main.go` and `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` in a single pass, implementing R1.1-R1.4 (three-column comparison output for two sorted files). The implementation should:\n   - Parse two file arguments, open them as line scanners\n   - Merge-compare lines lexicographically  \n   - Output to appropriate columns with tab indentation\n   - Handle file exhaustion by draining remaining lines\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPI